## Proposed/unexecuted implementation artifact

The visible fixture does not provide the existing application package path, package name, storage interfaces, exact-money type, or clearing-account identity. The patch below therefore assumes a new owned package at `internal/application/command`. Those names must be mapped to the real package before applying it.

The offset/clearing account is deliberately injected rather than invented. The production PostgreSQL implementation of `AtomicStore` is outside the assigned application-package scope; it must satisfy the documented single-transaction contract before this behavior can be considered production-complete.

